(2070751, 280463, 2780, '<td valign="top">I think the DoF looks very unnatural here. If you are going to fake blur in post processing, you should study the basic principles.<br/> <br/>The further something is away from the focal plane, the more it should be out of focus.<br/> <br/>Therefore the person closest to the camera should be more blurred than the person between them and the person in focus.<br/> <br/>Equally, the guy in green should be more out of focus than the people in blue cos he is further away from the girl in focus.<br/> <br/>Since you have created so much blur in such a small physical area, the background, which is much further away in comparison, should be completely out of focus and extremely blurred, so detail is hardly seen. This is one of the main things that gives away your blur is fake. The background is just as blurred as the other people, no more.<br/> <br/>Also, there seems to be very sloppy selection around the person in focus, since the trees in the background above her head are perfectly in focus! Also, some bits of her hat are out of focus despite being in the same focal plane as her.<br/> <br/>If you use Photoshop CS for editing there is a "Lens Blur" effect which will blur different amounts based on an alpha mask you can create. Basically, in focus things are white, and everything else is darker, with black being the most out of focus. You can paint gradients and objects in different shades of grey depending on how far away from the focal plane they are. Then the tool does all the blurring for you, and also can apply lens aperture effects to highlights, which does give a very different appearance to "Gaussian Blur".<br/> <br/>To sum up, blur is a gradual effect, not an "on and off" effect. You should try to experiment in photoshop to get the effect looking realistic before entering a shot here, or you will get a lot of people voting you down for bad editing.</td>', 'I think the DoF looks very unnatural here. If you are going to fake blur in post processing, you should study the basic principles. The further something is away from the focal plane, the more it should be out of focus. Therefore the person closest to the camera should be more blurred than the person between them and the person in focus. Equally, the guy in green should be more out of focus than the people in blue cos he is further away from the girl in focus. Since you have created so much blur in such a small physical area, the background, which is much further away in comparison, should be completely out of focus and extremely blurred, so detail is hardly seen. This is one of the main things that gives away your blur is fake. The background is just as blurred as the other people, no more. Also, there seems to be very sloppy selection around the person in focus, since the trees in the background above her head are perfectly in focus! Also, some bits of her hat are out of focus despite being in the same focal plane as her. If you use Photoshop CS for editing there is a "Lens Blur" effect which will blur different amounts based on an alpha mask you can create. Basically, in focus things are white, and everything else is darker, with black being the most out of focus. You can paint gradients and objects in different shades of grey depending on how far away from the focal plane they are. Then the tool does all the blurring for you, and also can apply lens aperture effects to highlights, which does give a very different appearance to "Gaussian Blur". To sum up, blur is a gradual effect, not an "on and off" effect. You should try to experiment in photoshop to get the effect looking realistic before entering a shot here, or you will get a lot of people voting you down for bad editing.', '2006-01-22 12:31:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(2070828, 281904, 7322, '<td valign="top">I like this. You did a good job singling out the main subject and that subject is actually interesting and engages the viewer. Good job!</td>', 'I like this. You did a good job singling out the main subject and that subject is actually interesting and engages the viewer. Good job!', '2006-01-22 12:54:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(2070838, 281501, 7322, '<td valign="top">THe subjects are signled out but unfortunately these people just don''t hold any interest for me. It''s just kind of boring.</td>', 'THe subjects are signled out but unfortunately these people just don''t hold any interest for me. It''s just kind of boring.', '2006-01-22 12:56:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(2070840, 281555, 7322, '<td valign="top">She''s singled out adn the background has some interest. I like the quality of the light in this photo. Ultimately, this lady just isn''t enough to engage my interest.</td>', 'She''s singled out adn the background has some interest. I like the quality of the light in this photo. Ultimately, this lady just isn''t enough to engage my interest.', '2006-01-22 12:57:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(2070861, 280547, 7322, '<td valign="top">I don''t really see her as being in a world of her own, which to me implies that she is lost in thought, since she is on a phone. But that''s just nitpicking about the title. I kind of like this. The thing I''m not sure about is that the blur looks like it was done with a filter which kind of ruins the effect a bit for me. I could be wrong--what is bothering me is that it looks like the floor is blurred in some areas and that doesn''t make sense to me. I''m not against post-processing for effect, and I''m a fan of motion blur, but something about this just doesn''t work for me.</td>', 'I don''t really see her as being in a world of her own, which to me implies that she is lost in thought, since she is on a phone. But that''s just nitpicking about the title. I kind of like this. The thing I''m not sure about is that the blur looks like it was done with a filter which kind of ruins the effect a bit for me. I could be wrong--what is bothering me is that it looks like the floor is blurred in some areas and that doesn''t make sense to me. I''m not against post-processing for effect, and I''m a fan of motion blur, but something about this just doesn''t work for me.', '2006-01-22 13:03:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(2070869, 280689, 7322, '<td valign="top">I kind of like this as a portrait but the two guys in the background don''t really give me the sense of a crowd.</td>', 'I kind of like this as a portrait but the two guys in the background don''t really give me the sense of a crowd.', '2006-01-22 13:05:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(2070872, 281356, 7322, '<td valign="top">He is singled out from the background but where is the crowd?</td>', 'He is singled out from the background but where is the crowd?', '2006-01-22 13:06:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(2070893, 281565, 7322, '<td valign="top">This set-up shot goes against the spirit of the challenge which was to "Drop your fear of candids this week" and single out a subject in a crowd. This certainly isn''t a candid, it isn''t even a crowd. It seems to be missing the point.</td>', 'This set-up shot goes against the spirit of the challenge which was to "Drop your fear of candids this week" and single out a subject in a crowd. This certainly isn''t a candid, it isn''t even a crowd. It seems to be missing the point.', '2006-01-22 13:13:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(2070899, 281515, 7322, '<td valign="top">I''m not getting the sense of a crowd here. I think you were to close to the subject. To me, this doesn''t show skill in isolating a subject from a crowd.</td>', 'I''m not getting the sense of a crowd here. I think you were to close to the subject. To me, this doesn''t show skill in isolating a subject from a crowd.', '2006-01-22 13:15:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(2070904, 281005, 7322, '<td valign="top">She stands out because she is dressed like the Statue of Liberty and that''s about it. I''m not getting a sense of her standing out from a crowd since the only other people (besides those that we can''t see in their cars) are the two kids on bikes.</td>', 'She stands out because she is dressed like the Statue of Liberty and that''s about it. I''m not getting a sense of her standing out from a crowd since the only other people (besides those that we can''t see in their cars) are the two kids on bikes.', '2006-01-22 13:17:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(2070909, 280431, 7322, '<td valign="top">Nice. It''s a candid, the umbrella adds some visual interest in terms of color and design (it also helps to isolate the subject) and this is definitely enough people to give me the sense of a crowd.</td>', 'Nice. It''s a candid, the umbrella adds some visual interest in terms of color and design (it also helps to isolate the subject) and this is definitely enough people to give me the sense of a crowd.', '2006-01-22 13:18:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(2070923, 280709, 7322, '<td valign="top">HUH? How does this connect to the challenge? Am I supposed to be interpreting the painting with the three figures as a crowd? The furniture? Is the pillow the subject? THe woman? I''m failing to see a focal point in this jumble. I don''t even get much of a sense of minimal depth of field. I don''t even understand the sentiment of the title. I''ve never seen a pillow as an object of abuse.</td>', 'HUH? How does this connect to the challenge? Am I supposed to be interpreting the painting with the three figures as a crowd? The furniture? Is the pillow the subject? THe woman? I''m failing to see a focal point in this jumble. I don''t even get much of a sense of minimal depth of field. I don''t even understand the sentiment of the title. I''ve never seen a pillow as an object of abuse.', '2006-01-22 13:23:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(2070933, 281945, 7322, '<td valign="top">I''m not getting a sense of crowd from these three guys (one of which isn''t even in the whole frame. The subject stands out to me more because she is naked and well-lit compared to her surroundings. I don''t get a sense that minimal depth of field was used.</td>', 'I''m not getting a sense of crowd from these three guys (one of which isn''t even in the whole frame. The subject stands out to me more because she is naked and well-lit compared to her surroundings. I don''t get a sense that minimal depth of field was used.', '2006-01-22 13:25:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(2070943, 281500, 7322, '<td valign="top">Where is the crowd? I think this might have been too much use of shallow depth of field. He seems to be isolated from his background but that background could be devoid of other people for all I can tell from this.</td>', 'Where is the crowd? I think this might have been too much use of shallow depth of field. He seems to be isolated from his background but that background could be devoid of other people for all I can tell from this.', '2006-01-22 13:27:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(2070969, 281015, 7322, '<td valign="top">I like this but I''m not sure if it quite works for the challenge. The focus in the background is actually quite sharp and my interest keeps being drawn to the two girls. He seems to be isolated more by his actual distance from the crowd and the fact that he is sitting and everyone else is walking. If the challenge had been simply to create a candid shot in which you isolate a single subject this would fit the challenge but minimal depth of field was specified.</td>', 'I like this but I''m not sure if it quite works for the challenge. The focus in the background is actually quite sharp and my interest keeps being drawn to the two girls. He seems to be isolated more by his actual distance from the crowd and the fact that he is sitting and everyone else is walking. If the challenge had been simply to create a candid shot in which you isolate a single subject this would fit the challenge but minimal depth of field was specified.', '2006-01-22 13:33:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(2070974, 281491, 7322, '<td valign="top">This is a nice candid shot but I don''t really get a sense that the subject is being isolated from a crowd. There is only one other discernable subject, perhaps two if I take the blur of a hat into consideration. Perhaps I am being to picky with these shots but I feel like ''crowd'' was a big part of the challenge.</td>', 'This is a nice candid shot but I don''t really get a sense that the subject is being isolated from a crowd. There is only one other discernable subject, perhaps two if I take the blur of a hat into consideration. Perhaps I am being to picky with these shots but I feel like ''crowd'' was a big part of the challenge.', '2006-01-22 13:36:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(2070988, 281300, 7322, '<td valign="top">This is a very nice shot but two people strolling by does not a crowd make. Also, you used selective desaturazition rather than minimal depth of field to isolate your subject. Some of the background has been blurred but not enough for me to consider it minimal depth of field. At any rate, the couple are focused just as sharply as the flutist and the idea was to single out a single subject from a crowd.</td>', 'This is a very nice shot but two people strolling by does not a crowd make. Also, you used selective desaturazition rather than minimal depth of field to isolate your subject. Some of the background has been blurred but not enough for me to consider it minimal depth of field. At any rate, the couple are focused just as sharply as the flutist and the idea was to single out a single subject from a crowd.', '2006-01-22 13:39:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(2070997, 281891, 32001, '<td valign="top">Nice shot, but I don''t see any reference to your subject being in a crowd.  Offset from the background nicely, but not singled out from a crowd.</td>', 'Nice shot, but I don''t see any reference to your subject being in a crowd.  Offset from the background nicely, but not singled out from a crowd.', '2006-01-22 13:41:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(2071026, 281990, 7322, '<td valign="top">This is a nice image. It seems to me that the subject is isolated less due to minimal DOF and more by the fact that the viewer can''t see the faces of the other sheep. This does isolate the subject from a crowd and I can see that minimal DOF was used but all the sheep could have been in focus and the main subject would still be isolated. I don''t know which way to go on this because it doesn''t seem like minimal DOF was the creative technique behind the photo. I do like the photo (although I feel like the main sheep''s face could be a bit sharper). I''ll give you the benefit of the doubt.</td>', 'This is a nice image. It seems to me that the subject is isolated less due to minimal DOF and more by the fact that the viewer can''t see the faces of the other sheep. This does isolate the subject from a crowd and I can see that minimal DOF was used but all the sheep could have been in focus and the main subject would still be isolated. I don''t know which way to go on this because it doesn''t seem like minimal DOF was the creative technique behind the photo. I do like the photo (although I feel like the main sheep''s face could be a bit sharper). I''ll give you the benefit of the doubt.', '2006-01-22 13:46:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(2071030, 281500, 51833, '<td valign="top">Because Stone Cold Said So!  Great capture.</td>', 'Because Stone Cold Said So!  Great capture.', '2006-01-22 13:47:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(2071054, 281537, 7322, '<td valign="top">"Drop your fear of candids this week and single-out a person in a crowd as your source of composition. Use minimal depth-of-field to your advantage to help isolate your subject, and as always, be creative."<br/> <br/>While you have been creative and you have used minimal DOF to isolate your main subject you ignored the main idea which was, from my understanding, to take a candid in a crowd. I few toys isn''t what I would call a crowd and it is debatable whether this is a candid rather than a posed shot.</td>', '"Drop your fear of candids this week and single-out a person in a crowd as your source of composition. Use minimal depth-of-field to your advantage to help isolate your subject, and as always, be creative." While you have been creative and you have used minimal DOF to isolate your main subject you ignored the main idea which was, from my understanding, to take a candid in a crowd. I few toys isn''t what I would call a crowd and it is debatable whether this is a candid rather than a posed shot.', '2006-01-22 13:52:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(2071060, 281891, 7322, '<td valign="top">"Drop your fear of candids this week and single-out a person in a crowd as your source of composition. Use minimal depth-of-field to your advantage to help isolate your subject, and as always, be creative."<br/> <br/>Where is the crowd in this shot? You''ve isolated the subject from her background but it is impossible to discern whether she is in a crowd or in her own backyard.</td>', '"Drop your fear of candids this week and single-out a person in a crowd as your source of composition. Use minimal depth-of-field to your advantage to help isolate your subject, and as always, be creative." Where is the crowd in this shot? You''ve isolated the subject from her background but it is impossible to discern whether she is in a crowd or in her own backyard.', '2006-01-22 13:53:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(2071065, 280253, 7322, '<td valign="top">Crowd? One guy way in the background is not a crowd. She is singled out because she is pretty much alone. This seems to have missed the point of the challenge.<br/> <br/>"Drop your fear of candids this week and single-out a *person in a crowd* as your source of composition. Use minimal depth-of-field to your advantage to help isolate your subject, and as always, be creative"</td>', 'Crowd? One guy way in the background is not a crowd. She is singled out because she is pretty much alone. This seems to have missed the point of the challenge. "Drop your fear of candids this week and single-out a *person in a crowd* as your source of composition. Use minimal depth-of-field to your advantage to help isolate your subject, and as always, be creative"', '2006-01-22 13:55:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(2071070, 281257, 7322, '<td valign="top">Crowd? You''ve used minimal depth of field but how is the kids mother and one other person a crowd? This beach looks deserted to me.</td>', 'Crowd? You''ve used minimal depth of field but how is the kids mother and one other person a crowd? This beach looks deserted to me.', '2006-01-22 13:56:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(2071084, 279654, 21611, '<td valign="top">A beautiful shot, very well done but... Where is the crowd? I wanted to give this a 9 or 10 but I felt that it would not be fair to the rest of the shots that submitted according to the guidelines. In any event a great shot all the same.</td>', 'A beautiful shot, very well done but... Where is the crowd? I wanted to give this a 9 or 10 but I felt that it would not be fair to the rest of the shots that submitted according to the guidelines. In any event a great shot all the same.', '2006-01-22 14:02:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(2071086, 280917, 7322, '<td valign="top">How is this a crowd?  The main subject seems to be isolated by color rather than minimal DOF.  This shot seems to miss the point of the challenge and I just don''t think it is very good.</td>', 'How is this a crowd?  The main subject seems to be isolated by color rather than minimal DOF.  This shot seems to miss the point of the challenge and I just don''t think it is very good.', '2006-01-22 14:02:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(2071088, 281843, 7322, '<td valign="top">Crowd? Am I the only person that needs more than one or two other people for a crowd? This is a nice portrait and you have isolated a subject from the background but there was more to the challenge then that--you were supposed to isolate a single subject from a *crowd*. One other girl does not make a crowd.  <br/> <br/>"Drop your fear of candids this week and single-out a person in a crowd as your source of composition. Use minimal depth-of-field to your advantage to help isolate your subject, and as always, be creative"</td>', 'Crowd? Am I the only person that needs more than one or two other people for a crowd? This is a nice portrait and you have isolated a subject from the background but there was more to the challenge then that--you were supposed to isolate a single subject from a *crowd*. One other girl does not make a crowd.   "Drop your fear of candids this week and single-out a person in a crowd as your source of composition. Use minimal depth-of-field to your advantage to help isolate your subject, and as always, be creative"', '2006-01-22 14:05:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(2071090, 280951, 7322, '<td valign="top">This is a nice portrait but the background is too blurred for me to get a sense that this man has been singled out from a crowd. He could be on an empty street for all I can tell.</td>', 'This is a nice portrait but the background is too blurred for me to get a sense that this man has been singled out from a crowd. He could be on an empty street for all I can tell.', '2006-01-22 14:07:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(2071096, 280589, 7322, '<td valign="top">Crowd? This figure is isolated because he is alone. This doesn''t even utilize minimal DOF. You were supposed to be creative but it should be within the boundaries of the challenge.<br/> <br/>"Drop your fear of candids this week and single-out a person in a crowd as your source of composition. Use minimal depth-of-field to your advantage to help isolate your subject, and as always, be creative"</td>', 'Crowd? This figure is isolated because he is alone. This doesn''t even utilize minimal DOF. You were supposed to be creative but it should be within the boundaries of the challenge. "Drop your fear of candids this week and single-out a person in a crowd as your source of composition. Use minimal depth-of-field to your advantage to help isolate your subject, and as always, be creative"', '2006-01-22 14:09:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(2071102, 281817, 7322, '<td valign="top">This is stretching the boundaries of the challenge but it squeaks by in my opinion because the idea is very clear from the photo (even without the title). <br/>I''m willing in this case to accept all the faces on the promos as a crowd since  the use of minimal DOF has effectively isolated the man from all those faces peering out at the viewer. Clever.</td>', 'This is stretching the boundaries of the challenge but it squeaks by in my opinion because the idea is very clear from the photo (even without the title). I''m willing in this case to accept all the faces on the promos as a crowd since  the use of minimal DOF has effectively isolated the man from all those faces peering out at the viewer. Clever.', '2006-01-22 14:11:15.000000', NULL, 1),
